{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":2,"author":{"id":"b3cab00338425c0da6d741f037644050ffaa3e47"},"timestamp":1580205296,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50Mjk4NDk1MzUxMw=="},"title":"Observations on inconsistent handling of relative paths in some commands","was":"Observations on inconsistent handling of relative paths across python commands"},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"b3cab00338425c0da6d741f037644050ffaa3e47"},"timestamp":1580205321,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50Mjk4NDk1NTA0NA=="},"title":"Observations on inconsistent handling of relative paths across python commands","was":"Observations on inconsistent handling of relative paths in some commands"},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1580207671,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI5ODUwODc3NjU="},"added":["relative paths"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1580207782,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3OTE4MjUwMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4098#issuecomment-579182500"},"message":"This is an absolutely crucial assessment. Thanks a lot for taking the time to do it!","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1580228737,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3OTMzNDM0MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4098#issuecomment-579334340"},"message":"\u003e Paths are interpreted as **relative** to the dataset root (specified as a string with `dataset=`) in following commands: [remove, drop, publish, siblings]\n\nNice to have a concrete list.  There are no real surprises here, and I'm glad none of the commands that have been updated for the new path handling (or rewritten entirely) show up here.\n\n\u003e I think I found an unrelated bug when I wanted to rerun a previous `run` command. It does not work when I pass the dataset as a string or -- interestingly -- also a dataset instance, but works if I use the command as a dataset method. When it \"fails\", the it just returns `No lines in history match specification`\n\nI think you're invoking IPython's magic command `rerun`:\n\n```\nIn [1]: pwd\nOut[1]: '/tmp'\n\nIn [2]: rerun(dataset=\"blah\")\nNo lines in history match specification\n\nIn [3]: rerun -gp\n=== Executing: ===\npwd\n=== Output: ===\nOut[3]: '/tmp'\n```\n\n\u003e instead of (what I think should be) complaining about a non-existent dataset.\n\nQuickly checking, I think things are working as you'd expect:\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003ererun\u003c/summary\u003e\n\n```sh\n#!/bin/sh\n\ncd \"$(mktemp -d --tmpdir dl-XXXXXXX)\"\n\ndatalad create a\n(\n    cd a\n    echo one \u003eone\n    datalad save\n    datalad run -i one -o out \"cat {inputs} \u003e\u003eout\"\n)\npython -c \"import datalad.api as dl; dl.rerun(since='')\"\npython -c \"import datalad.api as dl; dl.rerun(dataset='a', since='')\"\ncat a/out\n```\n\n```\n[INFO] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/dl-onXk5po/a \ncreate(ok): /tmp/dl-onXk5po/a (dataset)\nadd(ok): one (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n[INFO] Making sure inputs are available (this may take some time) \n[INFO] == Command start (output follows) ===== \n[INFO] == Command exit (modification check follows) ===== \nadd(ok): out (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  get (notneeded: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"\u003cstring\u003e\", line 1, in \u003cmodule\u003e\n  File \"/home/kyle/src/python/datalad/datalad/interface/utils.py\", line 492, in eval_func\n    return return_func(generator_func)(*args, **kwargs)\n  File \"/home/kyle/src/python/datalad/datalad/interface/utils.py\", line 480, in return_func\n    results = list(results)\n  File \"/home/kyle/src/python/datalad/datalad/interface/utils.py\", line 411, in generator_func\n    allkwargs):\n  File \"/home/kyle/src/python/datalad/datalad/interface/utils.py\", line 527, in _process_results\n    for res in results:\n  File \"/home/kyle/src/python/datalad/datalad/interface/rerun.py\", line 194, in __call__\n    purpose='rerunning a command')\n  File \"/home/kyle/src/python/datalad/datalad/distribution/dataset.py\", line 566, in require_dataset\n    raise NoDatasetArgumentFound(\"No dataset found\")\ndatalad.support.exceptions.NoDatasetArgumentFound: No dataset found\n[INFO] Making sure inputs are available (this may take some time) \n[INFO] == Command start (output follows) ===== \n[INFO] == Command exit (modification check follows) ===== \none\none\n```\n\n\u003c/details\u003e","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"b3cab00338425c0da6d741f037644050ffaa3e47"},"timestamp":1580229316,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3OTMzOTAxNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4098#issuecomment-579339014"},"message":"ha! thanks @kyleam and sorry for the noise! :)","files":null}]}